    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d730-a6">

                <pb facs="1321" n="1197" xml:id="pg1197"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 287.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Baker to Mr.
                            Saavedra.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-10-21"><hi rendition="#italic">October</hi> 21,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: Referring to your excellency’s two
                    notes to me, both of date the 9th instant, as also to your excellency’s note to
                    me of date the 18th instant, together with its inclosed statement bearing date
                    the 19th inst, I deem it proper to say that, to the desirable end of furnishing
                    a basis upon which it may be hoped that the Government of the United States may
                    regard itself justified in using its good offices in behalf of the Government of
                    Venezuela, I respectfully suggest that the Government of Venezuela propose to
                    pay, on the present provisional basis of distribution, to the several creditor
                    nations, the sum of 95,000 bolivars per month on the diplomatic reclamations,
                    and to pay in addition thereto, semi-annually, and on like basis of
                    distribution, all excess of the entire product of the 13 per cent, of the 40
                    unities which may accumulate over and above all the monthly payments of 95,000
                    bolivars each; this proposal to be provisional in its character; to go into
                    effect from and after its acceptance by the governments concerned, and to be
                    entirely independent of whether the Government of the United States may consent
                    or may not consent to receive and distribute the payments as proposed by the
                    Government of Venezuela.</p>
                <p>I with pleasure renew, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JEHU BAKER.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
